he function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [225 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [238 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [251 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [253 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [255 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [256 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [257 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [258 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [259 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [260 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [261 2 "// (fresh) keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes"] [270 2 "// held are the references mirrors hold on their items' handles because Go put the item there (a reference C"] [271 2 "// wrote into a slot is C's own): \"C holds the only reference\" (a brand-new object) is a count less these of 1"] [274 28 "// the mirrors a native (or a closure) used: synchronized to C when it returns"] [278 1 "// mirrorKind is the layout o's handle mirrors (0: a proxy's head only) and the bytes it needs."] [292 19 "// PyByteArrayObject (queue 270: PyByteArray_AS_STRING, GET_SIZE)"] [311 3 "// PySetObject (py-capi-1122: PySet_GET_SIZE reads used): fill 16, used 24, mask 32, table 40, hash 48, finger"] [312 3 "// 56, smalltable 64 (8 entries of 16 bytes), weakreflist 192"] [318 1 "// longDigits are an int's absolute value in CPython's 30-bit digits, least significant first (none for 0)."] [330 1 "// writeLong writes an int's PyLongObject fields at a (Include/cpython/longintrepr.h, 3.14: lv_tag is the digits'"] [331 1 "// count shifted by 3 with the sign in the low bits, 0 positive, 1 zero, 2 negative; then the digits)."] [349 1 "// asFloatValue is a float's (or a float subclass's instance's) value."] [363 1 "// newMirror writes o's layout at a (its handle, the head written) and records the mirror."] [382 31 "// ob_shash: -1, not computed"] [389 31 "// ob_hash: -1, not computed"] [396 31 "// hash: -1, not computed"] [401 1 "// syncToC writes the pyi value's state into its mirror (the slots Go changed: a new reference to the new item, the"] [402 1 "// old one's given back)."] [407 3 "// a set's size: fill and used (its table is Go's)"] [413 3 "// a bytearray: ob_size, ob_alloc, ob_bytes, ob_start (Include/cpython/bytearrayobject.h); its storage a block of"] [414 3 "// the world's, made again when it grows"] [496 1 "// syncFromC copies what C wrote into its mirror to the pyi value (the slots C changed; a NULL slot is a nil item, as"] [497 1 "// CPython's NULL until C fills it), and does so for the mirrors its items name, once an epoch."] [526 3 "// C's slots as last synchronized: C changed nothing, so Go's value stands (Python code a native ran may have"] [527 3 "// resized the list since: gh-72054's __index__ popping from it, test_slice's getindicesex_seq), written to C"] [528 3 "// when the native that uses it returns"] [560 10 "// resized from C: not provided (PyByteArray_Resize is a native)"] [583 1 "// holdRef and unholdRef are a mirror's reference to an item Go put in it, and its giving back."] [603 1 "// cOnly reports whether C holds the only reference to the handle h (its count, less the mirrors' own, is 1)."] [606 1 "// rawObj is the object a handle names without synchronizing it (nil for NULL)."] [615 1 "// freeMirror releases a mirror's own memory and its items' references (its handle released)."] [635 1 "// syncAllToC writes every mirror's pyi state into C (before the world is called: Python code may have changed any)."] [642 1 "// syncAllFromC copies every mirror's C state to its pyi value (when the world returns to Python)."] [650 1 "// nativeEnter and nativeLeave bracket a native's (or a closure's) run: what C wrote is copied to Go on the first use"] [651 1 "// of a mirrored object in it (fromHandle), and the mirrors it used are written back to C when it returns."] [672 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [681 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [683 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [684 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_basicsize bytes (and its items'), the built-in part a mirror of the"] [685 1 "// pyi value at its head, the extension's part C's after the base's size. The Go value is an instance of the type"] [686 1 "// keeping a built-in value, as a Python class deriving from the built-in keeps one; the record rides on it"] [687 1 "// (py.SetInstanceExt). Its memory lives as a C-born object's (queue 268): until Go collects the instance, then its"] [688 1 "// tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry."] [696 1 "// bornKind is the mirrored layout of t's built-in base (0: none of them)."] [709 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over int (its mirror a PyLongObject's)"] [712 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over an exception (no mirror: C reads its fields through functions)"] [718 1 "// bornOf is o's record when o is a C type's instance over a built-in base (nil: none)."] [730 1 "// bornHandle is such an instance's handle: its memory's address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the"] [731 1 "// C entry ends; its mirror written from Go, which may have changed it meanwhile) when it had left them."] [748 1 "// bornNew is tp_alloc for a C type over a built-in base: the instance of sub with nitems items (a tuple's or bytes'),"] [749 1 "// a new reference."] [776 1 "// bornValue is the built-in value of a C type's instance over a built-in base its base's __new__ makes from the"] [777 1 "// arguments (queue 270b: a spec over int without tp_new, HeapCTypeWithBasesSlot(5)): the base